	"description": [
		"This course explores Harlem, NY, focusing on the Harlem Renaissance, a major cultural movement from the 1920s and 1930s. In January, students attend music performances, cultural events, and site visits. These activities aim to deepen their understanding of this significant era through readings, guest lectures, archival research, and exploration. Students reflect on how, despite challenges related to power, class, race, and gender, the movement promoted progress in arts, ideas, and social change. Offered periodically during January term."
